---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import NoteCard from '../../components/NoteCard.astro';
import { leadershipNotes, leadershipReadings } from '../../lib/leadership';
const notes = leadershipNotes(await getCollection('notes'));
---

<Base
  title="Leadership & Organizations"
  description="Analysis by Swapnil Upganlawar on how generative AI changes management, team design, architecture, and accountability, with curated original readings."
>
  <div class="shell page-content leadership-page">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Leadership & Organizations / By Swapnil Upganlawar</p>
      <h1>
        AI changes the work.
        <br />
        <span>How should we lead?</span>
      </h1>
      <p>
        Original analysis on the choices behind AI adoption: how teams are
        organized, how people develop judgment, and who remains accountable for
        useful outcomes.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="#analysis">
          Explore the analysis <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
        </a>
        <a class="text-link" href="#reading-list">
          Curated readings <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div
      class="leadership-questions"
      aria-label="Questions this section explores"
    >
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / Management</p>
        <h2>What changes for managers?</h2>
        <p>
          Delegation, coaching, trust, and the choice of how to use time saved.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / Organization</p>
        <h2>Where does the work move?</h2>
        <p>
          Handoffs, review capacity, incentives, and the gap between faster
          tasks and better outcomes.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / Expertise</p>
        <h2>Who owns the whole system?</h2>
        <p>
          Architecture, decision rights, and accountability across people and AI
          tools.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <section
      id="analysis"
      class="leadership-analysis"
      aria-labelledby="analysis-heading"
    >
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">The analysis</p>
          <h2 id="analysis-heading">Decisions worth examining.</h2>
        </div>
        <a class="text-link" href="/writing/rss.xml">
          Follow my writing ↗
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="notes-grid">
        {notes.map((note) => (
          <NoteCard note={note} />
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="reading-list" aria-labelledby="reading-heading">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">The reading desk / Checked 21 September 2026</p>
          <h2 id="reading-heading">Go to the original thinking.</h2>
          <p class="section-intro">
            A curated starting point, with the kind of evidence and access made
            explicit.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ul class="leadership-readings">
        {leadershipReadings.map((reading) => (
          <li>
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">
                {reading.publisher} · {reading.date}
              </p>
              <h3>
                <a href={reading.url}>
                  {reading.title} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
                </a>
              </h3>
            </div>
            <div>
              <span class="pill">{reading.evidence}</span>
              <p>{reading.access}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>
    <aside class="leadership-method prose">
      <h2>Evidence, then interpretation.</h2>
      <p>
        The essays distinguish study findings, survey responses, analyst
        forecasts, and my proposed decision frameworks. Illustrations are
        labeled; a result from one task or company does not establish a
        universal organization design.
      </p>
      <p>
        Research and drafting are AI-assisted. This section is separate from
        automated briefings. Sources are linked for inspection, not as
        endorsements of Model Fieldnotes. See the{' '}
        <a href="/editorial/">editorial policy</a> or{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/swapupg/swapupg.github.io/issues/new?title=Leadership%20reading%20suggestion">
          suggest a source or correction
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Base>
